<h2>September 11-13: a price record becomes a presidential demand</h2>

<p>On September 11, the U.S. national average diesel price reached approximately $6.05 a gallon, according to AAA figures reported by The Washington Post. Ukraine also struck the Saratov refinery that night. [17] [18]</p>

<p>Wright's Fox interview recorded September 9 began to spread on social media beginning September 11 By September 13, Trump had made the refinery argument his own. [19]</p>

<p>On September 13, speaking at the Irish Open at his Doonbeg golf club, Trump said Zelensky should stop targeting Russian diesel infrastructure. His argument explicitly connected the attacks to harm beyond Russia. That same date, Ukraine reported strikes on the Slavyansk-ECO and TANECO refineries. [20] [21]</p>

<p>Later on September 13, Trump returned to the subject in his Air Force One press exchanges. He explained that he had asked Zelensky not to hit diesel plants and refineries.  [22] [23]</p>

